{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward bias when recent history shows volatility followed by a spike; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 1.5% to 3% during the first 7 days of the horizon.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00) but price history contains a single high-value outlier, the model fails to weight this as a mean-reversion signal and instead extrapolates linearly upward.",
    "Forecasts show significant lag in capturing immediate post-spike corrections; true outcomes often drop sharply within 5-8 days while models continue their initial upward trajectory.",
    "The model systematically underestimates volatility clustering, assuming smooth trends where actual EU ETS data exhibits high-frequency reversals after short-term rallies.",
    "Apply a downward correction factor of approximately -0.4 to the forecasted daily price when the last 3 days of history include a value >15% above the 18-day moving average and sentiment is neutral."
  ]
}
